# The Kidux package archive.
#
# Two suites, and the difference matters to a family: "stable" is what an
# installed machine follows and upgrades to unattended, "testing" is where a
# package lands the moment it builds. Nothing reaches stable without having been
# installed from testing on a real machine first.
#
# Each suite has its key. stable is signed with the archive's key, the one
# kidux-archive-keyring installs on a family's machine. testing is signed with
# the development key, which only a machine told to follow testing trusts: its
# public part is ci/archive/development-key.pgp, published beside the archive
# (ci/publish-local.sh).
#
# Origin is "Kidux" because that is what unattended-upgrades matches on; see
# apt/60kidux-unattended-upgrades in kidux-base.

